event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrocfw — \\\"greet, tested\\\" — outcome: campaign-met\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\nOn dev's branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit\\n`f0e572cd889fff5bd048007a7b08cc28ed15acf8` (on top of base `db35ac7e`):\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`:\\n  ```python\\n  def greet(name):\\n      return \\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"\\n  ```\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest-based tests covering a normal name\\n  (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\n## Verification (independent, not just dev's report)\\n\\nI fetched dev's branch into a separate worktree at the accepted commit and ran\\nthe exact required command myself:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nResult: exit code 0, `Ran 2 tests ... OK`. This matches dev's reported output.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- d001: both orchestrator and dev confirmed briefings (no code expected); accepted.\\n- d002: dispatched the mission's concrete requirements to dev in full (file\\n  paths, function contract, both required test cases, the exact verification\\n  command). Dev replied with commit hash, file contents, and test output.\\n  I fetched the branch, diffed the committed file contents against the\\n  requirement, and reran the test command myself in an isolated worktree\\n  before accepting.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nAll three stated mission criteria are satisfied:\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — present, correct.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — present, correct.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — confirmed independently.\\n\\nNo criteria remain unmet.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

